{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Female, creatinine 1.1 mg/dL.\n\nFor females, κ = 0.7, α = -0.241.\nSince Scr > κ (1.1 > 0.7), use max ratio = (1.1/0.7)^(-0.200).\n\n2021 CKD-EPI (no race):\neGFR = 142 × min(Scr/κ,1)^α × max(Scr/κ,1)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^Age × 1.012(if female)\n\n- min(1.1/0.7, 1) = 1, so min term^α = 1\n- max(1.1/0.7, 1) = 1.5714; raised to -1.200:\n  ln(1.5714) = 0.4520; ×(-1.2) = -0.5424; exp = 0.5814\n- 0.9938^33: ln(0.9938) = -0.006219; ×33 = -0.2052; exp = 0.8145\n- female factor 1.012\n\neGFR = 142 × 1 × 0.5814 × 0.8145 × 1.012\n= 142 × 0.5814 = 82.56\n× 0.8145 = 67.25\n× 1.012 = 68.06\n\nFINAL: 68"}